title ALES238 — lotus/catalog_verify, a catalog proven whole end to end
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first, send each finished increment, stop at custody gates
think The catalog family stands whole, and the named next Lotus crux (a signed carry — who made it) is a crypto seam gated on Keaton's word. The highest-Lindy NON-gated door is the cross-level deep verify: prove a whole body of work whole top to bottom.
think Each verify to date proved one level (verify_library at the catalog level, verify_album at the record level). verify_deep composes both over their public APIs — a Merkle check the shape of the catalog: the library digest binds each album manifest, each album manifest binds each bundle.
think AlbumTree pairs an album's name, its sealed album_manifest bytes, and the bundles it names. verify_deep runs verify_library first (catalog level, bounded AlbumIn array by max_albums), then opens each album manifest verify-before-trust and runs verify_album (record level). DeepError is the honest union of both error sets.
obs Witness proves five laws on metal, the key novelty being the record-tamper law — a single flipped bundle byte TWO LEVELS DOWN surfaces as TrackDigestMismatch while the catalog level stays clean. GREEN on the first metal pass; TAME style bans clean.
obs Pure composition, no new hash no new frame; content-addressing not a signature; no custody gate.
